<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n57336" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κίδναμαι</span></b> , 
			Pass.
		 of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κίδνημι</span> (only found in
		the compd. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπικ</span>-), poet. for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκεδάννυμαι</span>, used only in pres.
		and impf., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be
				spread abroad</i> or <i>over</i>, of the dawning day, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπεὶρ ἅλα κίδναται ἠώς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					23.227
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				8.1
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀδμὰ κατὰ χῶρον κ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					129.6
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κιδναμέναν μελιαδέα γᾶρυν</span>
			prob. in <i><span class="en">
				Simon.
				41
			</span></i>: once in Trag., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕπνος ἐπ᾽ ὄσσοις κ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hec.</u>
					916
				</span></i>
			 (lyr., 
				v.l. for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκίδ-</span>
			)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">; κολοιῶν κρωγμὸς . . κιδνάμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					7.713
				</span></i>
			 (Antip.).</div>
